# End-to-End Test Protocol (Mini-Pipeline)

The goal is to create a "Test Bench" script that exercises every single stage of the dubbing architecture (Stem Split -> Transcribe -> GPU Translate -> TTS -> GPU Lipsync -> Final Mix) on a miniature scale, completing in minutes rather than hours. This allows rapid iteration on translation prompts, TTS voices, and GPU settings without risking a 1-hour render.

## User Review Required

Please review the proposed workflow and provide feedback on the 30-second cutoff. Do you prefer a fixed duration (e.g. 30s) or a specific feature (e.g. automatically finding the first 30 seconds that actually contains dialogue)?

## Proposed Changes

We will introduce a dedicated testing script that hooks directly into the existing `pipeline.py` architecture.

### [NEW] [test_mini_pipeline.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/scripts/test_mini_pipeline.py)

We will create a script in a new `scripts/` directory that does the following:

1. **Clip Generation:** Accepts a 1-hour movie file and uses FFmpeg to extract exactly 30 seconds of video (from a timestamp you specify, defaulting to `00:00:20` to skip silent logos).
2. **Environment Injection:** Loads the isolated `get_env_with_ffmpeg()` to ensure the test runs under the exact same hardware conditions as the main app.
3. **Pipeline Submission:** Injects the 30-second clip directly into `pipeline.manager.add_job()` as a "testing" job.
4. **Console Telemetry:** Bypasses the Gradio UI and prints real-time status updates directly to your terminal, blocking until the `final_output.mp4` drops.

### [MODIFY] [README.md](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/README.md) (or Main Doc)

We will document the Test Protocol heavily, providing the exact terminal command to run the mini-pipeline. 

